<Layout title="Crisis Response Protocol — Don't Lose Your Way" description="How Don't Lose Your Way handles situations where a user may indicate risk of self-harm or suicide — honestly, including what it cannot do.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p>Effective Date: May 12, 2026</p>
      <p>This protocol describes how Don't Lose Your Way, operated by CC3PO LLC, handles situations where a user may indicate risk of self-harm or suicide. Our approach is realistic and honest about what we can and cannot do.</p>
      <p><strong>This platform is not a crisis intervention service.</strong> We do not have trained crisis counselors, mental health professionals, or 24/7 monitoring. Our response is limited to providing resources and blocking harmful content.</p>
      <p><strong>If you are in crisis right now:</strong></p>
      <p>Call or text 988 (U.S. Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline)</p>
      <p>Text TALK to 741741 (Crisis Text Line) | Call 911 for emergencies</p>
      <h1>What We Can Do</h1>
      <p>As a small operation, our crisis response is practical, not clinical:</p>
      <h3>1. Prominent Crisis Resources</h3>
      <p>The 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline is displayed prominently throughout the website — in the footer, on the disclaimer page, and in the Chapel area. These resources are always visible, not hidden behind a click.</p>
      <h3>2. Content Filtering in Submissions</h3>
      <p>Community voice submissions are reviewed before publication. Any submission that explicitly expresses intent to harm themselves or others is:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>Not published</li>
      <li>Reviewed by our team within a reasonable timeframe</li>
      <li>Replaced with a message directing the user to crisis resources</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>3. AI Safeguards</h3>
      <p>Our AI songwriting and reflection features are designed to:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>Never generate content that encourages self-harm or suicide</li>
      <li>Never provide instructions for self-harm</li>
      <li>Include crisis resource prompts if the system detects concerning input patterns</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Limitation:</strong> AI detection is not reliable and cannot replace human judgment. We do not guarantee that the AI will detect every concerning input.</p>
      <h3>4. No Automated Diagnosis</h3>
      <p>We do not use AI to diagnose, assess, or evaluate mental health conditions. AI on this platform generates creative content only — songs, reflections, and prompts. It does not perform risk assessments.</p>
      <h2>What We Cannot Do</h2>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>We cannot provide real-time crisis intervention.</strong> We do not have 24/7 monitoring or trained counselors</li>
      <li><strong>We cannot contact you directly.</strong> We do not collect personal information like email addresses or phone numbers, so we cannot reach out to check on you</li>
      <li><strong>We cannot guarantee AI will detect concerning content.</strong> AI is a creative tool, not a safety system</li>
      <li><strong>We cannot provide ongoing support.</strong> This is a creative reflection platform, not a therapeutic service</li>
      <li><strong>We cannot prevent all harmful content from being submitted.</strong> We review community submissions, but review is not instantaneous</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>How Community Voice Submissions Are Handled</h2>
      <p>When someone submits a community voice that indicates self-harm risk:</p>
      <p>1. The submission is held for review and not published immediately</p>
      <p>2. Our team reviews the submission within a reasonable timeframe</p>
      <p>3. If the submission contains explicit self-harm or suicidal intent, it is not published</p>
      <p>4. We cannot contact the person directly (submissions are anonymous) — so we ensure crisis resources are always visible on the site</p>
      <p>5. Repeated concerning submissions may result in IP-based access restrictions to protect the community</p>
      <h2>What You Should Do</h2>
      <p>If you are having thoughts of self-harm or suicide:</p>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>Call or text 988</strong> — U.S. Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline (24/7, free, confidential)</li>
      <li><strong>Text TALK to 741741</strong> — Crisis Text Line</li>
      <li><strong>Call 911</strong> — If you are in immediate danger</li>
      <li><strong>Go to your nearest emergency room</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Contact a trusted friend, family member, or mental health professional</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <p>You are not alone. Help is available.</p>
    </div>
